# render_distance_change.tas — change the render distance at runtime (C8).
#
# Purpose: the Settings picker changes the desired state of the chunk
# scheduler. The scheduler evicts the meshes past the new R + 1 and keeps
# loading.
#
# Usage (from utils/swindowzig). `--aa=none` puts Render Distance at row 6
# of the Video tab:
#   zig build native -Dexample=voxel
#   ./zig-out/bin/voxel --headless --aa=none --world=flatland \
#     --tas examples/voxel/tests/render_distance_change.tas 2>&1 \
#     | grep -E 'Render Distance|EVICT|CHUNK_STATS'
#   Expect "Render Distance -> 4" and "[EVICT] ... mesh(es) evicted".
#   Add --debug=on --debug-overlay=on --debug-page=pipeline
#   --dump-frame=/tmp/rd.ppm to see the chunk pipeline page of the debug
#   overlay (C12) after the scheduler is idle. A TAS key event has no
#   modifiers, so the TAS cannot press Ctrl+P.
#
# Tick numbering is relative to the first post-loading tick.

# --- Open the pause menu, go to Settings ---
5 keydown Escape
6 keyup Escape
10 keydown Down
11 keyup Down
15 keydown Enter
16 keyup Enter

# --- Down 6 times to Render Distance ---
20 keydown Down
21 keyup Down
24 keydown Down
25 keyup Down
28 keydown Down
29 keyup Down
32 keydown Down
33 keyup Down
36 keydown Down
37 keyup Down
40 keydown Down
41 keyup Down

# --- Left 8 times: 12 -> 4 ---
44 keydown Left
45 keyup Left
48 keydown Left
49 keyup Left
52 keydown Left
53 keyup Left
56 keydown Left
57 keyup Left
60 keydown Left
61 keyup Left
64 keydown Left
65 keyup Left
68 keydown Left
69 keyup Left
72 keydown Left
73 keyup Left

# --- Close the menu (Settings -> main -> game) ---
80 keydown Escape
81 keyup Escape
85 keydown Escape
86 keyup Escape

# --- Wait. The scheduler evicts and goes idle. ---
600 mouse_move 0 0
